KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ calls: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
no body for callee
--
A member of the partial specialization fn<R(Args...)> defined outside the
class gets no body in the specialization for an empty pack, fn<int()>;
fn<int(int)> gets it.  libc++'s std::function<int()>::operator() is
defined this way (cpp11_std_function_zero_argument and
cpp11_std_function_call_libcxx with libc++).
